{"type": "root", "attrs": {"index": "no"}, "body": [{"level": 0, "type": "title", "indent": 0, "text": ["Lens effects"], "extent": [12, 29]}, {"type": "warning_group", "body": [{"ext": null, "type": "warning", "indent": 0, "text": ["Old network"], "role": "item", "extent": [16, 38], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["As of Houdini 20.5, use ", {"scheme": null, "value": "/nodes/cop/index", "type": "link", "text": ["Copernicus nodes"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop/index.html"}, " instead of Compositing nodes. Though both networks still exist, the Compositing network is now designated as ", {"type": "code", "text": ["COP Network - Old"]}, ". The Compositing network and its nodes will be deprecated and then removed in a future Houdini release."], "extent": [38, 335]}], "container": true}], "container": true, "role": "item_group"}, {"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": ["Lens effects are very common and add extra realism or an artistic touch to images. Typical effects are lens distortion, chromatic aberration, vignetting and blur. The examples below provide workflows for distortion and vignetting."], "extent": [73, 305]}, {"level": 2, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 0, "text": ["Lens distortion"], "extent": [305, 327], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": ["Lens distortion uses a so-called ST map. ST maps are images where every pixel has a unique red and green color. The colors correspond to the screen space\u2019s X and Y coordinates. An ST map is the default state of the ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/uvmap", "type": "link", "text": ["UV Map COP"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/uvmap.html"}, " node."], "extent": [327, 579]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": ["The following example doesn\u2019t calculate a physically correct distortion from a real lens. The workflow only shows how to use an ST map for distortion effects. ST maps are typically provided by the matchmover or the lens manufacturer."], "extent": [579, 814]}, {"type": "ord_group", "body": [{"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["On the ", {"type": "em", "text": ["obj"]}, " level, create a ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/manager/cop2net", "type": "link", "text": ["COP2 Network"], "fullpath": "/nodes/manager/cop2net.html"}, " and double-click it to dive inside."], "extent": [814, 917]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["Inside the network, create an UV Map COP. This node represents the ST map."], "extent": [917, 994]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["On the ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Image"]}, " tab, change ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Override Size"]}, ", e.g. to ", {"type": "code", "text": ["1024, 1024"]}, "."], "extent": [994, 1066]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["From the ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Image Planes"]}, " dropdown, choose ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["P (xyz)"]}, "."], "extent": [1066, 1124]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["Set ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Raster Depth"]}, " to ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["32 Bit Floating Point"]}, "."], "extent": [1124, 1177]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["Add a ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/file", "type": "link", "text": ["File COP2"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/file.html"}, "."], "extent": [1177, 1213]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["Go to ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["File"]}, " and load the image you want to distort. The image in this example is a checker board and is shipped with Houdini. If you want to use this image as well, enter ", {"type": "code", "text": ["$HFS/houdini/pic/CheckerBoard.pic"]}, "."], "extent": [1213, 1427]}], "container": true}, {"level": 3, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 0, "text": ["Distortion image"], "extent": [1427, 1452], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 1, "text": ["Houdini requires a shape to calculate the amount of distortion for each pixel of the source image. You can use another image or a simple pattern like a circle, but also more complex geometry, for example a star."], "extent": [1452, 1667]}]}, {"type": "ord_group", "body": [{"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["Add a ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/shape", "type": "link", "text": ["Shape COP2"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/shape.html"}, ". This node defines the distortion shape."], "extent": [1667, 1745]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["On the ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Shape"]}, " tab, open the ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Shape Type"]}, " dropdown and choose ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Circle"]}, "."], "extent": [1745, 1825]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["Go to the ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Image"]}, " tab. For ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Override Size"]}, " enter the same values as on the UV Map COP2. There it was ", {"type": "code", "text": ["1024, 1024"]}, "."], "extent": [1825, 1946]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["A ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/xform", "type": "link", "text": ["Transform COP2"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/xform.html"}, " node scales the circle. Add the node and connect its ", {"type": "em", "text": ["first"]}, " input with the output of ", {"type": "code", "text": ["shape1"]}, "."], "extent": [1946, 2079]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["On the ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Transform"]}, " tab you can find the ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Scale"]}, " parameter. Set the values to ", {"type": "code", "text": ["1.3, 1.3"]}, ". Now, only the edges remain black."], "extent": [2079, 2208]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["Add a ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/blur", "type": "link", "text": ["Blur COP2"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/blur.html"}, " to soften the circle and avoid hard edges. Connect its ", {"type": "em", "text": ["first"]}, " input to the output of ", {"type": "code", "text": ["xform1"]}, "."], "extent": [2208, 2339]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["On the ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Blur"]}, " tab, set ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Size"]}, " to ", {"type": "code", "text": ["500"]}, ". This value creates a very soft shape."], "extent": [2339, 2424]}], "container": true}, {"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": ["This is how the distortion image should look."], "extent": [2424, 2471]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": [{"scheme": "Image", "value": "/images/distortionshape.jpg", "type": "img", "text": ""}], "extent": [2471, 2508]}, {"level": 3, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 0, "text": ["Deformation"], "extent": [2508, 2528], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": ["The next step calculates the checker board\u2019s distortion. This step requires two deformations. The first node uses the resized and blurred shape to deform the ST map. A second node uses the ST map\u2019s deformed pixel coordinates to deform the checker board image."], "extent": [2528, 2790]}, {"type": "ord_group", "body": [{"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["Add the first ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/deform", "type": "link", "text": ["Deform COP2"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/deform.html"}, ". Connect its ", {"type": "em", "text": ["first"]}, " input with the output of ", {"type": "code", "text": ["uvmap1"]}, ". The ", {"type": "em", "text": ["second"]}, " input is linked to the ", {"type": "code", "text": ["blur1"]}, " node\u2019s output."], "extent": [2790, 2952]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["Open the ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Deform"]}, " tab and go to ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Deform Plane"]}, ". In this node, the entry is ", {"type": "code", "text": ["C"]}, ". This corresponds with the UV Map\u2019s ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Image Planes"]}, " parameter."], "extent": [2952, 3101]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["from the ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Deform"]}, " dropdown, choose ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Shift by UV Gradient"]}, " to use the UV/ST map\u2019s color values to calculate the amount of distortion per pixel."], "extent": [3101, 3250]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": [{"type": "ui", "text": ["Scale"]}, " determines the amount of distortion. Enter ", {"type": "code", "text": ["2.5, 2.5"]}, " to get a visible effect."], "extent": [3250, 3342], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["The second Deform COP2 brings everything together and perform the actual calculation."], "extent": [3342, 3433]}], "container": true}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["Add the second Deform COP2. Connect its ", {"type": "em", "text": ["first"]}, " input with the output of the File COP2 with the checker board image. The ", {"type": "em", "text": ["second"]}, " input is linked to the first Deform node\u2019s output."], "extent": [3433, 3616]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["This node deforms the ", {"type": "code", "text": ["P"]}, " plane of the checker board. On the ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Deform"]}, " tab, go to ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Deform Plane"]}, " and enter ", {"type": "code", "text": ["P"]}, "."], "extent": [3616, 3733]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["Set ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Deform"]}, " to ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["To New UV Values"]}, " to transfer the ST map\u2019s pixel coordinates."], "extent": [3733, 3818]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["From the ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Image Wrap"]}, " dropdown, choose ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Clamp"]}, ". This clamps the incoming UV values at 0 or 1."], "extent": [3818, 3919]}], "container": true}, {"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": ["The image below shows the final effect on the checker board."], "extent": [3919, 3981]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": [{"scheme": "Image", "value": "/images/distortionresult.jpg", "type": "img", "text": ""}], "extent": [3981, 4019]}]}]}, {"level": 2, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 0, "text": ["Lens vignetting"], "extent": [4019, 4041], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": ["Vignettes are caused by a loss of lens efficiency towards a the edges of a lens. Most lenses are spherical and therefore, vignettes are typically circular. But, you normally notice a stronger effect along the shorter side of the frame: the film gate\u2019s rectangular shape fits inside the circle and the shorter side is closer to the edge of the lens. For anamorphic lenses, you can squeeze the vignette accordingly."], "extent": [4041, 4457]}, {"type": "ord_group", "body": [{"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["On the ", {"type": "em", "text": ["obj"]}, " level, create a ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/manager/cop2net", "type": "link", "text": ["COP2 Network"], "fullpath": "/nodes/manager/cop2net.html"}, " and double-click it to dive inside."], "extent": [4457, 4560]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["Add a ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/file", "type": "link", "text": ["File COP2"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/file.html"}, "."], "extent": [4560, 4596]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["Go to ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["File"]}, " and load the image you want to distort. The image in this example is a checker board and is shipped with Houdini. If you want to use this image as well, enter ", {"type": "code", "text": ["$HFS/houdini/pic/CheckerBoard.pic"]}, "."], "extent": [4596, 4810]}], "container": true}, {"level": 3, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 0, "text": ["The vignette"], "extent": [4810, 4831], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": ["The lens determines the vignette\u2019s shape and in most cases it\u2019s a circle."], "extent": [4831, 4907]}, {"type": "ord_group", "body": [{"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["Add a ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/shape", "type": "link", "text": ["Shape COP2"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/shape.html"}, ". This node defines the vignette\u2019s shape."], "extent": [4907, 4985]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["On the ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Shape"]}, " tab, open the ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Shape Type"]}, " dropdown and choose ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Circle"]}, "."], "extent": [4985, 5065]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["Go to the ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Image"]}, " tab. For ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Override Size"]}, " enter the same values as on the UV Map COP2. There it was ", {"type": "code", "text": ["1024, 1024"]}, "."], "extent": [5065, 5186]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["From the ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Raster Depth"]}, " dropdown, choose ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["32 Bit Floating Image"]}, "."], "extent": [5186, 5258]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["A ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/xform", "type": "link", "text": ["Transform COP2"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/xform.html"}, " node scales the circle. Add the node and connect its ", {"type": "em", "text": ["first"]}, " input with the output of ", {"type": "code", "text": ["shape1"]}, "."], "extent": [5258, 5391]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["On the ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Transform"]}, " tab you can find the ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Scale"]}, " parameter. Set the values to ", {"type": "code", "text": ["1.05, 1.05"]}, " to make the circle/vignette slightly bigger."], "extent": [5391, 5532]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["Add a ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/blur", "type": "link", "text": ["Blur COP2"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/blur.html"}, " to soften the circle and avoid hard edges. Connect its ", {"type": "em", "text": ["first"]}, " to input the output of ", {"type": "code", "text": ["xform1"]}, "."], "extent": [5532, 5663]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["On the ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Blur"]}, " tab, set ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Size"]}, " to ", {"type": "code", "text": ["300"]}, "."], "extent": [5663, 5710], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 4, "text": ["Cropping cuts away the enlarged parts of the circle and creates a clean vignette."], "extent": [5710, 5797]}], "container": true}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["Add a ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/crop", "type": "link", "text": ["Crop COP2"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/crop.html"}, " and connect its input with the output of ", {"type": "code", "text": ["blur1"]}, "."], "extent": [5797, 5882]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["From the ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Crop"]}, " dropdown, choose ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["By Offset, Width & Height"]}, "."], "extent": [5882, 5950]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["Set ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Units"]}, " to ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Pixels"]}, "."], "extent": [5950, 5981]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["The values for ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Horizontal Crop"]}, " and ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Vertical Crop"]}, " must cover the entire image area. In this example, the checker board\u2019s size is ", {"type": "code", "text": ["1024"]}, " by ", {"type": "code", "text": ["1024"]}, ". The corresponding crop values are therefore ", {"type": "code", "text": ["0, 1024"]}, " for both parameters."], "extent": [5981, 6213]}], "container": true}, {"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": ["What you have now is a blurred white circle on a black background."], "extent": [6213, 6281]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": [{"scheme": "Image", "value": "/images/vignetteshape.jpg", "type": "img", "text": ""}], "extent": [6281, 6316]}]}, {"level": 3, "id": null, "container": true, "type": "h", "indent": 0, "text": ["Applying the vignette"], "extent": [6316, 6346], "body": [{"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": ["You can now add the blurred circle shape to the checker board image to create vignette effect."], "extent": [6346, 6443]}, {"type": "ord_group", "body": [{"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["Add a ", {"scheme": "Node", "value": "/nodes/cop2/colorcorrect", "type": "link", "text": ["Color Correct COP2"], "fullpath": "/nodes/cop2/colorcorrect.html"}, " node. Connect its ", {"type": "em", "text": ["first"]}, " input with the output of the checker board\u2019s File node. The ", {"type": "em", "text": ["second"]}, " input is linked to the ", {"type": "code", "text": ["crop1"]}, " node. "], "extent": [6443, 6628]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["At the moment you can\u2019t see any effect. To combine vignette mask and image, you must multiply the images. On the ", {"type": "code", "text": ["colorcorrect1"]}, " node\u2019s ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Color Correct"]}, " tab and go to ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Master \u25b8 Mult"]}, ". To see the vignette, set the RGB values to ", {"type": "code", "text": ["0.2, 0.2, 0.2"]}, ", for example. What you get is a large dark area with bright edges."], "extent": [6628, 6943]}, {"blevel": 2, "type": "ord", "indent": 0, "text": ["To fix the colors, open the ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Mask"]}, " tab and turn on ", {"type": "ui", "text": ["Invert Mask"]}, "."], "extent": [6943, 7016]}], "container": true}, {"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": ["Below you can see the result from the example\u2019s values and images."], "extent": [7016, 7084]}, {"type": "para", "indent": 0, "text": [{"scheme": "Image", "value": "/images/vignetteresult.jpg", "type": "img", "text": ""}], "extent": [7084, 7118]}]}]}], "title": ["Lens effects"], "included": ["/composite/_old_cops_deprecated"]}